  System.Raylib.C.adam - raylib's C API (Ramon Santamaria, zlib license,
  6.2: windows, input, 2D / 3D drawing, textures, fonts, models, audio),
  written by `adam cimport` from the headers libraylib.a is built with
  (res/libs/vendor/include/raylib: raylib.h, raymath.h, rlgl.h) with their
  own names: every routine `external "raylib"` (libraylib.a in
  res/libs/vendor/<triple>, built by AdamLang-Libs), records laid out as C
  lays them out, the constant macros as typed consts, raymath's inline
  routines translated into Adam. raylib's own link list (its
  LibraryConfigurations.cmake + its bundled GLFW) is the unit's
  @linklibrary list, per target: GLFW opens OpenGL's library at run time on
  linux, so only libX11 (six routines raylib's objects name) is linked
  there. Do not edit: a change belongs in the spec,
  res/cimport/System.Raylib.C.cimport.toml, then regenerate.
